## Why This Is Asked
This question tests building a DP over subsequences with constraints, requiring a clear state definition and transition over previous indices, plus reconstruction capabilities.

## Key Concepts
- Subsequence DP with constraints
- State dp[i] and parent tracking
- Time/space analysis and reconstruction

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxSubseqWithDiff(a, d) {
  const n = a.length;
  const dp = Array(n).fill(0);
  const par = Array(n).fill(-1);
  let best = -Infinity, bestIdx = -1;

  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    dp[i] = a[i];
    for (let j = 0; j < i; j++) {
      if (Math.abs(a[i] - a[j]) <= d && dp[j] + a[i] > dp[i]) {
        dp[i] = dp[j] + a[i];
        par[i] = j;
      }
    }
    if (dp[i] > best) {
      best = dp[i];
      bestIdx = i;
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct subsequence
  const seq = [];
  let curr = bestIdx;
  while (curr !== -1) {
    seq.push(curr);
    curr = par[curr];
  }
  return { maxSum: best, subsequence: seq.reverse() };
}
```

## Time/Space Complexity
Time: O(n²) due to nested loops checking all previous indices
Space: O(n) for dp and parent arrays

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to craft DP with interval constraints and reconstruction using palindromic substrings.

## Key Concepts
- Palindromic substring precomputation in O(n^2)
- DP over prefix length and exact count: dp[i][t]
- Transition considers ending a palindrome at i with start p
- Reconstruction requires backpointers to recover substrings

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxPalSubstr(s, k) {
  const n = s.length;
  const isPal = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(n).fill(false));
  for (let i = n - 1; i >= 0; --i) {
    for (let j = i; j < n; ++j) {
      if (s[i] === s[j] && (j - i < 2 || isPal[i+1][j-1])) isPal[i][j] = true;
    }
  }
  const NEG = -1e9;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const par = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
      dp[i][t] = Math.max(dp[i][t], dp[i-1][t]);
      if (t > 0) {
        for (let p = 0; p < i; p++) {
          if (isPal[p][i-1]) {
            const val = dp[p][t-1] + (i - p);
            if (val > dp[i][t]) { dp[i][t] = val; par[i][t] = p; }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
  // Reconstruction would trace par[] to extract substrings
}
```

